Dear Saral Jalan,

This is a draft proposal for limited Architectural Services to creating a builder’s permit set for the Gardena lot, assuming that the duplex plans are similar/ mirrored and interior kitchen layout and general finishes will be selected by builder.


Description:

The property is a XXXX sf lot in Gardena. The project is to create a small-lot subdivision with 6 parcels via SB 684, or SB 1123 if the lot is large enough. The project includes a 3-story duplex with two car garages for each unit, roughly 2500 sf, on each of the 6 parcels.  Shi Architect (“Architect”) will be working with the client (“Owner”) and Owner’s Consultants to prepare construction drawings.


Scope of Work and Services:

Phase I - Concept and Schematic Design
-	Provide site and zoning analysis for property.
-	Test fits will be provided by others. 

Phase II – Design Development
-	Coordinate with Owner’s consultants, including Civil, Landscape, and Structural.
-	Prepare drawings for Gardena Planning for Tentative Vesting Map and Site Plan Review, including the items below:
o	Architectural Site.
o	Architectural Floor plans.
o	Architectural Elevations and finishes
o	Tentative Tract Map by Owner’s Civil Engineer
-	Address required changes with owner to obtain planning approval.

Phase III – Construction Drawings
-	Create a simplified Construction Drawing Set and submit to Gardena Building and Safety, and LA County Fire Prevention Plan Checks, including the items below:
o	Architectural site plans, floor plans, elevations, sections, details, and door/ window schedules.
o	T-24 energy calculations, as coordinated with Owner’s MEP engineer.
o	Coordinated Civil, Landscaping, Structural, and MEP drawings. 
-	Assist Owner to obtain approvals for other permitting clearances. 
-	Address plan check corrections for each agency to obtain approvals to obtain Ready to Issue (RTI) status. 


Clarifications and Exclusions:

1.	Additional costs may be required if this project entitlement is not ministerial or requires public review.
2.	Professional services by other disciplines, such as Civil, Landscaping, Structural, Mechanical, Plumbing, and Electrical are excluded from this scope of work. 
3.	Fire Sprinklers will be design-build and be considered as a deferred submittal.
4.	Owner is responsible for engaging consultants separately as required for this project, including Survey, Soils Report, Hydrant Flow Test, and other specialty studies or reports required by the reviewing agencies.
5.	Construction Administration services are excluded from this scope of work. These services may be provided as additional services upon written agreement.
6.	Physical plotting to be reimbursed separately.
7.	Scopes of Work not included above may be included as additional services with Client’s written agreement.
8.	Additional Services may be provided at an hourly rate of $150/hr.


Billing and Payment: 
The fee for this project is $65,000. Invoices will be issued upon reaching the following milestones:

